{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 20,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am a sun sneezer. Which is also known as having the photic sneeze reflex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4800,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or, the autosomal dominant compelling helio ophthalmic outbursts syndrome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10000,
    "dDurationMs": 7460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which basically means if I go from a dark area into somewhere that's brightly lit -  You know, like, looking at the sun - I will sneeze."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18430,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wait for it..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34320,
    "dDurationMs": 2209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There you go, I'm a sun sneezer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41100,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why does this happen?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44760,
    "dDurationMs": 3619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People have known about this effect for at least a few thousand years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48960,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Aristotle was probably a sun sneezer because in his book of problems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53220,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he asked: Why does the sun provoke sneezing?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57420,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And his answer was it was the heat from the sun which causes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60120,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sweating inside your nose, and so you sneeze to get rid of the moisture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67710,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a couple millennia later"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69260,
    "dDurationMs": 6119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sir Francis Bacon demonstrated that this could not be the case because when he closed his eyes and turned towards the sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75420,
    "dDurationMs": 6199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well he did not experience that photic sneeze reflex so his explanation was that it was the eyes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81869,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "watering and then when some of that moisture got down into the nose that caused the tickle which makes you sneeze"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87330,
    "dDurationMs": 5479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but even this theory has its problems because eye watering is a much slower process than the photic sneeze reflex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93420,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it can't be the cause. Before I started researching sun sneezing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98420,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I thought that having the photic sneeze reflex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100860,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Must Convey some sort of evolutionary advantage under the people who have it. If you think about it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105690,
    "dDurationMs": 6199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sneezing is a way of transmitting disease. In your snot there can be the living Bacteria that cause"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112710,
    "dDurationMs": 7580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tuberculosis, and strep throat or viruses that cause measles mumps Rubella and influenza, so if you're living in a moist dark cave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120290,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you sneeze"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121290,
    "dDurationMs": 6559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where your snot lands on the floor or the walls of the cave and those Pathogens can stay alive for hours or even days"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128369,
    "dDurationMs": 4309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increasing the Likelihood of spreading that disease to other people who live with you in your cave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133170,
    "dDurationMs": 6709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whereas if you only sneeze when you emerge from the darkness of the cave and into bright sunlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140280,
    "dDurationMs": 5809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, then that mucus will quickly dry out or because it's exposed to the harmful UV rays of the sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146100,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It will kill all of those pathogens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149420,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Greatly decreasing the risk of spread of disease"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152820,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the 1960s some studies were revealing the hereditary nature of the photic sneeze reflex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158879,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was a father who would sneeze two times when he entered bright sunlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163730,
    "dDurationMs": 3899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when they tested his baby daughter who was just four weeks old"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167880,
    "dDurationMs": 3889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Moving her from a dark room into full sunlight also caused her to sneeze"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172260,
    "dDurationMs": 4039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Exactly two times and by the 1980s it was clear that this trait was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176460,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "autosomal dominant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177600,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meaning that you only needed to inherit one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180320,
    "dDurationMs": 3779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Copy of the Gene from just one of your parents in order to exhibit the trait"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184200,
    "dDurationMs": 7970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when studies the population have been done only about 18 to 35 percent of people actually have the photic sneeze reflex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192990,
    "dDurationMs": 6770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I don't really think this gives a great evolutionary advantage, otherwise everyone would have it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200190,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know it could just be one of those random mutations that happens over time and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204900,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sustains itself because it's neither good nor bad evolutionarily speaking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209340,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it affects roughly one in four people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212010,
    "dDurationMs": 2329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can you spot the person with the photic sneeze reflex?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215940,
    "dDurationMs": 6980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nowadays, it's actually been found that the gene responsible for the photic sneeze reflex is on the second chromosome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222920,
    "dDurationMs": 4319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's a single letter of DNA that's been changed, on my second chromosome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227240,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have a C"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228480,
    "dDurationMs": 6529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where non sun sneezers have a T, and the reason that we know this is that back in 2010 there was a study of about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235350,
    "dDurationMs": 2179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10,000 people where they went online and they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237720,
    "dDurationMs": 3589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reported whether they were sun sneezers or not and then their DNA was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241410,
    "dDurationMs": 6860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "analyzed and the groups were compared and what they found was the thing the sun sneezers had in common was this one particular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248820,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "letter change in their DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251280,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That I think is pretty amazing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254820,
    "dDurationMs": 6260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now it's unclear exactly how this change affects your physiology and makes you more susceptible to sun sneezes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261150,
    "dDurationMs": 6290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the best theory at the moment is that it involves the trigeminal nerve which is the largest cranial nerve it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267720,
    "dDurationMs": 3769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Involves all of the feeling that you have in your face and as the name implies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271490,
    "dDurationMs": 6180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It actually has three branches one of which receives stimuli from your eye and another which receives stimuli from your nose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277950,
    "dDurationMs": 6049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the thought is that this really active stimulation of the optic nerve may cross over into the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284100,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maxillary Branch causing that little tickle which gets you to sneeze"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288150,
    "dDurationMs": 6950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Photic Sneezes are generally pretty harmless unless you're doing something like flying a fighter jet or performing some sort of delicate surgery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295860,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this methodology,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297280,
    "dDurationMs": 7339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can allow us to learn a lot about different heritable traits and diseases just by studying lots of people and their genotypes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309099,
    "dDurationMs": 7400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode of veritasium was supported by 23andme. Which is actually the company that figured out that gene polymorphism"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317139,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "responsible for the photic Sneeze reflex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319539,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the name of the Company 23andme comes from the fact that humans actually have 23 pairs of chromosomes and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325659,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The purpose of the company is to give people insight into their own DNA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329379,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what you do is spit into a vial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332099,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is actually much harder than it sounds and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335439,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Send it off to them and of course in your saliva are some of the cells from your mouth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339659,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They analyze the DNA from those cells"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341789,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then they send you a report where you can find out tons of stuff about your genes like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346840,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where do your genes come from that is what's your ancestry and do you have the photic sneeze reflex? Do we share the same?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354279,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Change of DNA on our second chromosome you can also learn about your health and other physical traits and how much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361810,
    "dDurationMs": 4429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Neanderthal you are so if you want to learn more about your genotype"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366339,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you should go to 23andme.com/veritasium, so I want to thank 23andme for supporting me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372300,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, I want to thank you for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
